              "name": "text",
              "value": "ENGINEERING KNOWLEDGE BASE  DEPLOYMENT CHECKLIST  Before deploying a new release:  1. Make sure all automated tests are passing. 2. Confirm the pull request has been reviewed and approved. 3. Merge the approved code into the main branch. 4. Check that all required environment variables are configured. 5. Run the application build successfully. 6. Deploy first to the staging environment. 7. Perform a quick smoke test on staging. 8. Check application logs for errors. 9. Get final approval before production deployment. 10. Deploy to production. 11. Run another smoke test after deployment. 12. Monitor logs and important metrics for at least 15 minutes. 13. If a serious problem appears, follow the rollback procedure.  PR REVIEW GUIDELINES  When reviewing a pull request:  1. Make sure the PR has a clear title and description. 2. Understand what problem the PR is trying to solve. 3. Check that the code is easy to read and maintain. 4. Look for unnecessary complexity or duplicated code. 5. Check for possible bugs and edge cases. 6. Make sure error handling is included where needed. 7. Check for security or privacy problems. 8. Confirm tests have been added or updated. 9. Make sure existing tests are still passing. 10. Check that no secrets, API keys, or passwords were committed. 11. Leave clear and respectful review comments. 12. Approve the PR only when important issues have been resolved.",
